+# BLUE CURRENT V51.15.0 — PEAK-SERVICE STRESS & FAILURE TESTING
+
+V51.11–V51.15 adds controlled peak-service rehearsal across 10 operational pressure/failure scenarios:
+
+1. Reservation burst
+2. High occupancy / seating pressure
+3. Rapid table turns
+4. Mid-service staff change
+5. Kitchen pressure
+6. Delayed requests
+7. API failure
+8. Connector / partial dependency failure
+9. Reconnect and retry
+10. Partial degradation and recovery
+
+## Test evidence model
+
+Every scenario result requires human-recorded evidence.
+
+Failure/reconnect scenarios require additional human-recorded recovery evidence before PASS is accepted.
+
+Blue Current never turns a missing result, expected behavior, or plausible metric into a PASS.
+
+Each result stores:
+
+- scenario
+- PASS / FAIL
+- actor / timestamp
+- evidence
+- recovery evidence when required
+- prerequisite snapshot
+- override state/reason
+- observed latency
+- observed errors
+- observed duplicate count
+- `operationalMutationPerformed: false`
+- `syntheticPass: false`
+
+## Controlled rehearsal parameters
+
+Each stress run records:
+
+- target occupancy %
+- reservation burst count
+- target table-turn minutes
+- simulated latency
+- baseline restaurant capacity model
+
+## Current authenticated Chefs runtime
+
+Status:
+
+`peak-service-stress-ready`
+
+Across five in-scope restaurants:
+
+- 50 total scenarios
+- 0 passed
+- 0 failed
+- 50 not yet executed
+
+Marina Grille currently has prerequisite evidence for all 10 stress scenarios.
+
+Harbor House, River & Rail, The Cabin, and Garden Social expose prerequisite gaps across their scenario set because their current authoritative restaurant configuration still lacks required floor/workforce/kitchen/dependency evidence.
+
+This is readiness evidence, not a failure result. A scenario does not become PASS or FAIL until a human records the controlled rehearsal outcome.
+
+## Missing prerequisites
+
+A controlled rehearsal may deliberately test a known missing prerequisite, but it requires a documented override reason. The missing prerequisite remains in the captured evidence.
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- simulation does not mutate operations
+- results are human recorded
+- recovery evidence required for failure-scenario PASS
+- synthetic passes prohibited
+- prerequisite overrides require reasons
+- automatic retry execution false
+- automatic failure recovery false
+- automatic scenario PASS false
+- autonomous production changes false
+
+## Validation
+
+- V51.15 focused stress lifecycle PASS
+- all 10 scenario classes exercised PASS
+- recovery-evidence guard PASS
+- prerequisite override guard PASS
+- V51.10 regression PASS
+- authenticated stress endpoint PASS
+- authoritative DB unchanged
+- undefined module exports: 0
+- duplicate HTML IDs: 0
+- npm run check PASS
+- 926 JavaScript files
+- 776 client scripts
+- 5,792 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V51.16–V51.20 — Data Integrity & Recovery
+
+- reservation integrity
+- guest/floor/staff/kitchen state integrity
+- duplicate prevention
+- refresh/reload survival
+- server restart persistence
+- interrupted write behavior
+- retry/idempotency verification
+- reconnect reconciliation
+- partial failure recovery
+- corruption/drift detection
+- recovery certification
